These configurations demonstrate that a combination of moderate dimensionality, two layers, and careful tuning of the learning rate and number of clusters can lead to high performance. The use of aggressive node addition with a lower scaling factor also shows promise in balancing class distributions effectively.

By focusing on these promising combinations, future trials can be designed to further refine and optimize the model for better generalization and robustness.
